```javascript
function reverseAdjectiveOrder(sentence) {
  // Split the sentence into words using a space delimiter
  const words = sentence.split(' ');

  // Initialize empty arrays for adjectives and other words
  const adjectives = [];
  const others = [];

  // Iterate through each word and determine if it's an adjective
  for (const word of words) {
    const partOfSpeech = getPartOfSpeech(word);

    if (partOfSpeech === 'adjective') {
      adjectives.unshift(word);
    } else {
      others.push(word);
    }
  }

  // Combine the arrays back into a sentence
  const reversedSentence = others.join(' ') + ' ' + adjectives.join(' ') + ' ';

  return reversedSentence;
}
// Helper function to determine the part of speech of a word using Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK)
function getPartOfSpeech(word) {
  const posTagger = new window.nlp('en', {tagger: true});
  const result = posTagger.tag(word)[0];
  return result ? result.pos : null;
}
```
This function uses the Natural Language Toolkit (NLTK) library to determine the part of speech of each word in the sentence. If a word is identified as an adjective, it is added to the beginning of the `adjectives` array. All other words are added to the `others` array. Finally, the arrays are combined back into a sentence with the order of adjectives reversed.

